{"paper_id":"paper_46f6118697c6397c","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"ev_doc_5eb0affa079c_000086_16ffc984dc9a","source":"SI section 2/Table S1 assigns compound 2 to CCDC 2512981 and reports formula C18H14B2N6O12F12S4."},{"evidence_id":"ev_doc_ced2213a1270_000186_5497c9505d81","source":"Main paper data-availability/crystallographic statement cites CCDC 2512981-2512983."},{"evidence_id":"ev_doc_ced2213a1270_000133_97a25df0559c","source":"Main paper PDF p.4 assigns compound 2's dominant absorption chiefly to HOMO-4 to LUMO and gives 323 nm and f=0.4243. Its printed 4.33 eV is inconsistent with that wavelength and with SI Table S3. A numerical typo is likely, but no author-confirmed correction is established; this energy is not a numeric target."},{"evidence_id":"ev_doc_ced2213a1270_000134_06926d150144","source":"Main paper continuation interprets the compound-2 orbital ordering in terms of electron-withdrawing triflate substituents and N6-related orbitals."},{"evidence_id":"ev_doc_5eb0affa079c_000117_00e0873d52bb","source":"SI computational-study section states Gaussian 16, B3LYP/6-31+G(d), SMD dichloromethane and DFT-D3BJ for optimization and TD-DFT."},{"evidence_id":"ev_doc_5eb0affa079c_000119_e84fb1c9ec64","source":"SI PDF p.18, Table S3 compound-2 state list: S5 = 3.8436 eV, 322.58 nm, f=0.4243. These remain the evaluator targets, confirmed on 2026-09-23 after original-page and raw-calculation comparison; independent verification values are corroboration, not replacement targets. See paper_route.md section 5 for the comparison."},{"evidence_id":"ev_doc_5eb0affa079c_000120_1cc9e6f995dd","source":"SI PDF p.18, Table S3 assigns the dominant 217 to 222 configuration coefficient 0.70241 to S5. Figure S22 on the same page labels HOMO-4 (217), HOMO (221) and LUMO (222)."}]}
